# SOLNP_plus

A derivative-free C solver for nonlinear optimization with constraints.

This source release is prepared for COIN-OR onboarding review (2026-10-01-r2).
It is intended for optimization researchers, students and application developers.

- Project home: https://github.com/COPT-Public/SOLNP_plus
- Project manager: Tianhao Liu
- Contact: tianhao.liu@sjtu.edu.cn
- Declared owner of project-owned code: Dongdong Ge (see OWNERSHIP.txt).
- License: MIT for project-owned code; component terms in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.
- Support / bug reports / feature requests: https://github.com/COPT-Public/SOLNP_plus/issues
- Code of conduct: https://www.coin-or.org/code-of-conduct/
- Reference paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.07160

## Build, install and test

Prerequisites: C compiler, CMake >=3.20, BLAS/LAPACK, Python 3 and NumPy. Bundled OSQP 0.6.3/QDLDL is built automatically. MATLAB and a GPU are not needed.
Read INSTALL, then run `bash build.sh` from this directory.

Success is process exit 0; failures return nonzero. Tests, their expected answers,
acceptance tolerances and extension instructions are described in tests/README.md.
Small models are included in examples/. VALIDATION.md records the actual tested
configuration and results. These checks do not constitute a performance benchmark
or validation of all optional interfaces.

## Package layout

- source/: source and retained upstream material.
- build.sh and tests/: documented build/installation checks and regression tests.
- examples/: analytic examples with expected solutions.
- AUTHORS and CITATION.txt: authorship and paper references.
- LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and OWNERSHIP.txt: license and ownership scope.
- SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json and CHANGES_FOR_COIN_OR.txt: revision and changes.
The package does not claim COIN-OR acceptance.
The project manager is the designated maintenance and contribution-review contact.
